    "question_type": "conceptual",
    "question_text": "What are the various types of pollution caused by industries and their reasons?",
    "question_latex": null,
    "mcq_options": [],
    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Industries are responsible for air, water, land, and noise pollution. Air pollution is caused by undesirable gases like sulphur dioxide and carbon monoxide. Water pollution results from industrial wastes and effluents. Thermal pollution occurs when hot water is discharged into water bodies. Land pollution is due to dumping of harmful wastes, and noise pollution arises from industrial activities and machinery.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, industries contribute to various types of pollution including air, water, land, and noise.",
